block 2729.13 153.754 24 0 0 0 0 1000 0
> \text A box draws because it defines a function of two variables. A picture is what a map from the plane looks like: one pixel for every input, coloured by what comes out -- viridis for a real, the colour itself for a vec3, hue and lightness for a complex number. Its knobs are uniforms, so they reshape the picture without rebuilding, and the wheel over it zooms the patch of the plane on show.
end
